{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_held_out", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable", "claim": "The missed ventricular fibrillation episode represents a failure of reliability and risk reduction under EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1.", "support_note": "Directly cites the requirement to reduce risks in case of a single fault condition.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-art83-pms-system", "claim": "The post-market surveillance system must actively gather data on device performance and safety.", "support_note": "Cites the obligation to systematically analyze quality, performance, and safety throughout the device lifetime.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "claim": "The missing confidence-score log prevents definitive attribution of cause or confirmation of recurrence.", "support_note": "Artifact exists but content is described as 'missing' in the narrative; cannot verify specific data points.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A", "claim": "Static analysis reports do not support a causal link to this telemetry failure.", "support_note": "Explicitly stated as synthetic and for an unrelated module.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A", "claim": "Static analysis reports do not support a causal link to this telemetry failure.", "support_note": "Explicitly stated as synthetic and for an unrelated module.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.52, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident involves a single missed detection of ventricular fibrillation in real-time telemetry, which constitutes a failure in a safety-critical function (monitoring and alerting for life-threatening arrhythmia). Under EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1, devices must ensure reliability such that 'in the event of a single fault condition... appropriate means shall be adopted to eliminate or reduce as far as possible consequent risks.' A missed detection represents exactly this type of risk-reduction failure. While no adverse outcome occurred and only one episode was reported (preventing Severity 4 based on realized harm), the potential for serious patient harm if such an event were not contained by automatic controls is significant, warranting a minimum of Severity 3.\n\nHowever, confidence is low (0.52) because: (1) The confirmatory device confidence-score log for the exact episode window is missing from ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A and ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A; without this data, we cannot definitively attribute the miss to a specific code change or verify if it was an isolated incident versus part of a broader degradation pattern. (2) The static analysis reports (ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A and ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A) are explicitly noted as synthetic for unrelated modules, providing no causal link to the telemetry logic failure.\n\nPer governance feedback, a confirmed field safety corrective action cannot be issued without confirmatory evidence of recurrence or deployed-population impact. The current data supports only an investigation into whether this single miss was due to a regression in the detection algorithm (requiring human review for root cause analysis) rather than immediate recall actions.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "74d7dcc4be15c66ad8154919f5d724a03b1ddf46b455a29dc8565f66e300a631", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0030", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0030_r3", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0030", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T19:09:12.671682Z", "total_steps": 6, "trace_id": "813aedc7-ae01-4c93-bb23-6ea82c0ac431"}
